# University Course Catalog MCP Server

A production-grade Model Context Protocol (MCP) server providing access to a university course catalog with tools for searching courses, retrieving prerequisites, looking up instructors, and visualizing prerequisite dependency graphs.

## Overview

This project implements an MCP server that exposes a university course catalog through the Model Context Protocol. It enables AI assistants and LLM-based applications to:

- **Search courses** by keyword across course codes, titles, and descriptions
- **Get direct prerequisites** for any course
- **Look up instructors** by name
- **Visualize complete prerequisite graphs** showing all transitive dependencies
- **Access course descriptions** and **department directories** as resources
- **Compare courses** using structured prompts

The server uses FastAPI for HTTP transport, SQLAlchemy with SQLite for data persistence, and the official MCP Python SDK for protocol compliance.

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client[MCP Client / LLM / Inspector] -->|Streamable HTTP| MCP[MCP Server<br/>FastAPI + MCP SDK]
    MCP --> Tools[Tools]
    MCP --> Resources[Resources]
    MCP --> Prompts[Prompts]
    Tools --> Services[Service Layer]
    Resources --> Services
    Prompts --> Services
    Services --> Repos[Repository Layer]
    Repos --> DB[(SQLAlchemy + SQLite)]
```

## Features

### Tools

| Tool | Purpose | Input |
|------|---------|-------|
| `search_courses` | Search catalog by keyword | `query` (string), `department_code` (optional string) |
| `get_prerequisites` | Get direct prerequisites | `course_code` (string) |
| `lookup_instructor` | Find instructor by name | `instructor_name` (string) |
| `get_prerequisite_graph` | Full dependency graph | `course_code` (string) |

### Resources

| Resource | URI | Description |
|----------|-----|-------------|
| Course Descriptions | `resource://course_descriptions` | All courses with code, title, and description |
| Department Directory | `resource://department_directory` | All departments with names and codes |

### Prompts

| Prompt | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `course_comparison_template` | Structured template for comparing two courses |
| `course_advisor` | Academic advising prompt for course planning |

## Tech Stack

- **Python** 3.12
- **MCP** (Model Context Protocol) Python SDK 1.6+
- **FastAPI** 0.115+ for HTTP transport
- **Uvicorn** ASGI server
- **SQLAlchemy** 2.0 ORM
- **SQLite** database
- **Pydantic** 2.9 for validation
- **NetworkX** 3.4 for graph algorithms
- **pytest** for testing
- **Docker** for containerization

